{
  "beruf": "einzelhandel",
  "title": "Shops and supermarkets",
  "level": "A2–B1",
  "reviewed": false,
  "_note": "spanish-for-work run, 2026-11-07: written by hand for Spain, read once by an AI second reader, not yet by a human. translations.en = English meaning; deHint = German translation (the 'German' tab). Words already in the lexicon or in another deck are refs, with this job's own example and sense. Working conditions are general orientation only.",
  "intro": "Supermarkets and small shops hire a lot of people in Spain, for the till, the shelves and the counters. This deck has the shop and its parts, what you do during a shift, offers and returns, safety and security, and what to say to customers and colleagues. Most shops say tú to younger customers and usted to older ones.",
  "introEasy": "Do you work in a shop or supermarket in Spain? Learn the words for your work here.",
  "jobs": [
    "Cajero/a",
    "Reponedor/a",
    "Dependiente/a",
    "Charcutero/a",
    "Frutero/a",
    "Vendedor/a"
  ],
  "tipps": [
    "At the counter, the key question is «¿Quién va ahora?» or «¿Quién es el siguiente?». Customers at Spanish markets also ask «¿Quién da la vez?» to find their place in the queue.",
    "The words you will say all day: «¿Tiene tarjeta de cliente?», «¿Quiere bolsa?», «¿Con tarjeta o en efectivo?», «¿Me deja ver el ticket?»",
    "If a customer complains and you don't know what to do, call the person in charge: «Un momento, por favor. Aviso al encargado.»"
  ],
